{"name":"Rosewood Dreams","hex":"#ebbeb5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rosewood","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The fragrant wood of Dalbergia nigra, a Brazilian tree in the legume family, which has a sweet smell.","Any of several dozen woods, resembling that of Dalbergia nigra in some respect."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rosewood"},{"term":"dreams","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of dream"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of dream"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dreams"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rosewood","blocks":[{"text":"Rosewood is any of a number of richly hued hardwoods, often brownish with darker veining, but found in other colours. It is hard, tough, strong, and dense. True rosewoods come from trees of the genus Dalbergia, but other woods are often called rosewood. Rosewood takes a high polish and is used for luxury furniture-making, flooring, musical instruments, and turnery."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Rio-Palisander%2C_dunkel_Holz.JPG/330px-Rio-Palisander%2C_dunkel_Holz.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosewood","wikidata":"Q122421"},{"title":"Dream","blocks":[{"text":"A dream is a succession of images, dynamic scenes and situations, ideas, emotions, and sensations that usually occur involuntarily in the mind during certain stages of sleep. Humans generally spend more than two hours dreaming per night, and each dream lasts around 5–20 minutes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/A_dream_%28BM_1868%2C0808.9057%29.jpg/330px-A_dream_%28BM_1868%2C0808.9057%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dream","wikidata":"Q36348"},{"title":"Shades of red","blocks":[{"text":"Varieties of the color r